{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' tests/test_own_records_guard.py; sed -n '60,125p' tests/test_self_tenancy.py; sed -n '420,510p' tests/test_spec_gate.py; sed -n '1,120p' attest/specs/237/spec.md; git show e5de67dbc0094fd327c01b5532a94c2770361a49:attest/specs/237/spec.md | sed -n '1,120p'; git log --oneline --decorate 0661d6813864ef6a70e670906128287c7fad85a7..cb35e66c7677273ebcf09b5f9e4449043589f20a\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Issue #210: `test` inherits a records-only commit's result only because\nno test in the ordinary suite reads this repository's own records\ndirectory, the one thing such a commit changes. The tests that do are\nmarked @pytest.mark.own_records and are the only ones `test` runs on the\ninherit path, the only ones the doctor job runs, and the ones every\nother run excludes (-m 'not own_records'). This guard is what keeps the\nmarker true: an unmarked test that names this repository as the tenant\na product reader is pointed at, or joins ROOT to the records directory,\nfails here. Nothing is exempt: the doctor's own proofs carry the marker\nsince #229 build-04, when a hand-kept deselect list that stood in for\nit was missing one test and the gate ran that test against the running\nbuild's own marker.\n\nThe guard reads test source for the vocabulary by which a test in this\nsuite reaches the repository's own tree (ROOT handed to a product reader,\nROOT joined to \"attest\" or to the manifest's paths). It cannot follow a\nhelper that hides ROOT; a new way of reaching the records adds a pattern\nhere. The property behind the list was also checked directly when this\nguard was written: the suite run on a copy of the repository with\nattest/records removed, unmarked tests only, passed.\n\nRun: python3 -m pytest tests -q\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ast\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nTESTS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nMARK = \"pytest.mark.own_records\"\nREADERS = (\n    re.compile(r\"\\b(?:run_doctor|drive_report|read_manifest|run_attavo)\\(\\s*ROOT\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"\\bROOT\\s*/\\s*[\\\"']attest[\\\"']\"),\n    re.compile(r\"\\bROOT\\b[^\\n]*\\bpaths\\b\"),\n)\n\n\ndef _is_marked(node: ast.AST) -> bool:\n    decorators = getattr(node, \"decorator_list\", [])\n    return any(ast.unparse(d) == MARK for d in decorators)\n\n\ndef unmarked_own_records_readers(tests_dir: Path, skip: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"`file::test` for every test in tests_dir that reads the repository's\n    own records without the marker. `skip` is a file name not scanned: this\n    file states the patterns as strings and would name itself.\"\"\"\n    found: list[str] = []\n    for path in sorted(tests_dir.glob(\"test_*.py\")):\n        if path.name == skip:\n            continue\n        source = path.read_text()\n        tree = ast.parse(source)\n        if MARK in source and any(\n                isinstance(n, ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t, ast.Name) and t.id == \"pytestmark\"\n                                                  for t in n.targets) and MARK in ast.unparse(n.value)\n                for n in tree.body):\n            continue\n        for node in ast.walk(tree):\n            if not isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) or not node.name.startswith(\"test_\"):\n                continue\n            if _is_marked(node):\n                continue\n            body = ast.get_source_segment(source, node) or \"\"\n            name = f\"{path.name}::{node.name}\"\n            if any(pattern.search(body) for pattern in READERS):\n                found.append(name)\n    return found\n\n\ndef test_no_unmarked_test_reads_this_repositorys_own_records() -> None:\n    assert unmarked_own_records_readers(TESTS, skip=Path(__file__).name) == []\n\n\ndef test_every_doctor_proof_test_carries_the_marker() -> None:\n    \"\"\"The doctor's proofs read this repository's own records by\n    construction (run_doctor(ROOT)); the guard above names any that lose\n    the marker, and this names the set so a new proof's test is written\n    marked (#229 build-04).\"\"\"\n    source = (TESTS / \"test_doctor.py\").read_text()\n    tree = ast.parse(source)\n    proofs = [n.name for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef)\n              and n.name.startswith(\"test_\") and \"run_doctor(ROOT)\" in (ast.get_source_segment(source, n) or \"\")]\n    assert len(proofs) >= 7, proofs\n    unmarked = [n.name for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef) and n.name in proofs and not _is_marked(n)]\n    assert unmarked == [], unmarked\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"reader\", [\n    \"run_doctor(ROOT)\",\n    \"drive_report(ROOT, m, item)\",\n    \"read_manifest(ROOT)\",\n    \"run_attavo(ROOT, 'report')\",\n    \"list((ROOT / 'attest').rglob('*.json'))\",\n    \"sorted((ROOT / m['paths']['records']).iterdir())\",\n])\ndef test_the_guard_names_a_planted_reader_and_not_a_marked_one(tmp_path: Path, reader: str) -> None:\n    (tmp_path / \"test_planted.py\").write_text(\n        f\"def test_reads() -> None:\\n    {reader}\\n\")\n    (tmp_path / \"test_marked.py\").write_text(\n        f\"import pytest\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.own_records\\ndef test_reads() -> None:\\n    {reader}\\n\")\n    (tmp_path / \"test_module_marked.py\").write_text(\n        f\"import pytest\\n\\npytestmark = pytest.mark.own_records\\n\\n\\ndef test_reads() -> None:\\n    {reader}\\n\")\n    assert unmarked_own_records_readers(tmp_path, skip=\"\") == [\"test_planted.py::test_reads\"]\n\n\ndef test_the_guard_leaves_a_test_that_builds_its_own_tenant_alone(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    (tmp_path / \"test_own.py\").write_text(\n        \"def test_builds(tmp_path):\\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, 'valid')\\n    run_doctor(root)\\n\")\n    assert unmarked_own_records_readers(tmp_path, skip=\"\") == []\n    # boundary path. Verified by simulating the merge locally.\n    # Item 227 added [doctor].built_since, the window for proof seven; [doctor].from\n    # stays absent for the reason above.\n    assert set(m.get(\"doctor\") or {}) == {\"built_since\"}, m.get(\"doctor\")\n    assert m[\"forge\"][\"checks_command\"]\n    assert m[\"forge\"][\"file_issue_command\"]\n    paths = m[\"spec\"][\"boundary\"][\"paths\"]\n    assert \"bin/**\" in paths and \"attavo/**\" in paths, paths\n    assert \"spec\" in m[\"gates\"]\n    assert m[\"gates\"][\"spec\"][\"retires\"]\n    assert m[\"tests\"][\"select\"]\n    assert m[\"tests\"][\"run\"]\n    assert m[\"operators\"][\"approvers\"]\n    assert m[\"checks\"][\"command\"]\n\n\ndef test_tests_run_and_the_test_job_exclude_the_own_records_tests_by_marker() -> None:\n    \"\"\"The tests that read this repository's own records -- the doctor's\n    proofs among them -- must never run inside an item's gate or the\n    test job: a proof no item has satisfied yet, or one that reads the\n    running build's own marker, fails a build for nothing (#229\n    build-04: the gate ran the whole suite and\n    test_no_invocation_lacks_record read build-04's own .started marker\n    as a dead invocation). They are told apart by @pytest.mark.own_records\n    and by nothing else: [tests].run and ci.yml's test job carry\n    -m 'not own_records', the doctor job and the inherit path carry\n    -m own_records, and no --deselect names a test anywhere. Three\n    hand-copied lists did this before and one was missing a test.\"\"\"\n    m = load_manifest()\n    assert \"-m 'not own_records'\" in m[\"tests\"][\"run\"], m[\"tests\"][\"run\"]\n    assert \"--deselect\" not in m[\"tests\"][\"run\"], m[\"tests\"][\"run\"]\n    assert \"--deselect\" not in m[\"checks\"][\"command\"], m[\"checks\"][\"command\"]\n    if \"pytest\" in m[\"checks\"][\"command\"]:\n        assert \"-m 'not own_records'\" in m[\"checks\"][\"command\"], m[\"checks\"][\"command\"]\n    ci = (ROOT / \".github\" / \"workflows\" / \"ci.yml\").read_text()\n    assert \"--deselect\" not in ci\n    assert \"python3 -m pytest tests -q --durations=5 -m 'not own_records'\" in ci\n    assert ci.count(\"python3 -m pytest tests -q -m own_records\") == 2, \"the inherit path and the doctor job\"\n\n\ndef run_select_tests(stdin_text: str) -> list[str]:\n    run = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(SELECT_TESTS)], input=stdin_text,\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    return [line for line in run.stdout.splitlines() if line]\n\n\ndef test_select_tests_maps_bin_attavo_to_the_whole_suite() -> None:\n    assert run_select_tests(\"bin/attavo\\n\") == [\"tests\"]\n\n\ndef test_select_tests_maps_an_adapter_path_to_the_adapter_tests() -> None:\n    selected = run_select_tests(\"adapters/example/run\\n\")\n    assert \"tests/test_adapters.py\" in selected and \"tests/test_executor_conformance.py\" in selected\n    assert \"tests\" not in selected, \"an adapter path selected the whole suite\"\n\n\ndef test_select_tests_maps_a_schema_path_to_the_record_and_attest_tests() -> None:\n    selected = run_select_tests(\"schema/records/build.schema.json\\n\")\n    assert \"tests/test_record_schemas.py\" in selected and \"tests/test_attest.py\" in selected\n    assert \"tests\" not in selected, \"a schema path selected the whole suite\"\n\n\ndef test_select_tests_maps_an_unrelated_path_to_nothing() -> None:\n    assert run_select_tests(\"README.md\\n\") == []\n\n\n    amend_problem(root)\n\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"spec-gate\", \"1\")\n    assert run.returncode == 0\n\n    rec = latest_record(root, \"1\", \"spec\")\n    assert rec[\"status\"] == \"pass\"\n    assert rec[\"criteria\"] == [{\"name\": \"checks_marker.sh\", \"on_tree\": 1, \"on_stub\": 0}]\n    assert rec[\"refusal\"] is None\n\n\ndef add_bucket_line(root: Path, bucket: str) -> None:\n    spec_md = root / \"specs\" / \"1\" / \"spec.md\"\n    text = spec_md.read_text().replace(\"## Problem\\n\", f\"## Problem\\n\\nBucket: {bucket}\\n\", 1)\n    spec_md.write_text(text)\n    commit_all(root, f\"name bucket {bucket}\")\n\n\ndef test_spec_gate_refuses_a_bucket_the_tenant_does_not_list_and_passes_a_listed_one(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Root-cause buckets (#229 build-04 and the convergence ruling of\n    2026-09-27): a fix item names the bucket its change closes as one\n    'Bucket: <slug>' line in its problem, and the gate refuses a slug the\n    tenant's buckets.md (beside the specs directory) does not list, or a\n    line with no such file. Written red first: on v0.30.0 the line is\n    prose and the gate passes it.\"\"\"\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    add_bucket_line(root, \"shared-working-copy\")\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"spec-gate\", \"1\")\n    assert run.returncode == 1, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    rec = latest_record(root, \"1\", \"spec\")\n    assert rec[\"status\"] == \"refused\"\n    assert rec[\"refusal\"] == \"bucket: shared-working-copy named but buckets.md does not exist\", rec[\"refusal\"]\n    assert rec[\"criteria\"] == [], \"refused before any criterion ran\"\n\n    (root / \"buckets.md\").write_text(\n        \"# buckets\\n\\n- liveness-by-proxy: a pid stood in for the holder\\n\")\n    commit_all(root, \"list one bucket\")\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"spec-gate\", \"1\")\n    assert run.returncode == 1\n    assert latest_record(root, \"1\", \"spec\")[\"refusal\"] == \"bucket: shared-working-copy is not listed in buckets.md\"\n\n    (root / \"buckets.md\").write_text(\n        \"# buckets\\n\\n- liveness-by-proxy: a pid stood in for the holder\\n\"\n        \"- shared-working-copy: one checkout, many writers\\n\")\n    commit_all(root, \"list the bucket\")\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"spec-gate\", \"1\")\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    rec = latest_record(root, \"1\", \"spec\")\n    assert rec[\"status\"] == \"pass\" and rec[\"refusal\"] is None\n\n\ndef test_spec_gate_leaves_a_spec_with_no_bucket_line_alone(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A capability item has no bucket; the check is on the line, not on\n    every spec, and a tenant with no buckets.md is not asked for one.\"\"\"\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    assert not (root / \"buckets.md\").exists()\n    assert run_attavo(root, \"spec-gate\", \"1\").returncode == 0\n## Problem\n\nBucket: dogfood-tests-told-apart-by-a-list\n\nItem #229's fourth attempt ran 3,375 s and cost $2.62 to fail on one test. The executor's change touched `attavo/common.py` and `attavo/build.py`, `select-tests` mapped that to the whole suite, and the gate ran `tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_invocation_lacks_record` in its worktree, where that test read build-04's own `.started` marker as a dead invocation. The test is one of the seven that read this repository's own records and belong to the doctor job alone. It was the one the deselect lists did not name.\n\nThere were three of those lists: `[tests].run` in the manifest, the `test` job in `ci.yml`, and `DESELECT_FLAGS` in `tests/test_self_tenancy.py`, each naming six tests by hand, kept equal by a test that counted them, and a fourth in the doctor job's `-k` expression naming five. Meanwhile the marker that says what these tests are, `@pytest.mark.own_records`, already existed: the inherit path runs `-m own_records` alone, and `tests/test_own_records_guard.py` fails any unmarked test that reads the repository's own records, with the six listed tests exempted precisely because the list stood in for the marker. Two mechanisms, disjoint sets, and the list was the one that went stale. A list a person copies is prose; a marker on the test is the fact.\n\nThis is the first fix item filed under the convergence ruling of 2026-09-27: defects are classified by the root cause that made them possible, each fix closes a bucket by making the state unrepresentable rather than adding a check, and the number read over time is the count of distinct buckets, not of symptoms. The item carries the mechanism with it.\n\nOne marker, no list. The six doctor tests gain `@pytest.mark.own_records` beside the one that had it. `[tests].run` becomes `xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q -m 'not own_records'`, `ci.yml`'s full-suite step carries the same expression, and the doctor job's step becomes `python3 -m pytest tests -q -m own_records`, the same step the inherit path already runs. Every `--deselect` in the manifest and the workflow goes, `DESELECT_FLAGS` and its test go, the guard's exemption and the test that counted the list go. What remains is the guard, which now exempts nothing, and one new test naming the set: every test in `test_doctor.py` that calls `run_doctor(ROOT)` carries the marker. `attavo test` uses `[tests].run` and so inherits the expression; an executor that names a marked test by hand gets nothing run, which is right.\n\nThe bucket line. A fix item's spec names its bucket as one line in the problem, `Bucket: <slug>`. The tenant's closed list is `buckets.md` beside its specs directory (`attest/buckets.md` here), one bucket per line, `- <slug>: <one sentence>`. `attavo spec-gate` refuses a spec whose bucket line names a slug the file does not list, or names any slug when the file does not exist, before any criterion runs; a spec with no bucket line is not asked for one, since a capability item has no bucket. Adding a bucket is an item's own act in the same change as its fix. The count is read with `grep -h '^Bucket:' attest/specs/*/spec.md | sort | uniq -c`; it becomes a subcommand when it moves a decision and not before. This repository's `attest/buckets.md` lists the five buckets the ruling named, with their specimens.\n\nNot in this item: the driver's records-only commits, the classifier's order, the marker's pid, the adapter's tools (buckets 1, 5, 4 and 2, each its own item); any change to what the doctor's proofs assert; the analyze read of bucket counts.\n\nRetires: three hand-copied deselect lists and the test that counted them; the doctor job's `-k` list; the guard's exemption; symptom-grain fix items without a named bucket.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/spec.py\n- attavo/cli.py\n- attavo.toml\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- attest/buckets.md\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n- tests/test_own_records_guard.py\n- tests/test_self_tenancy.py\n- tests/test_ci_inherit.py\n- tests/test_spec_gate.py\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- the-own-records-tests-are-told-apart-by-the-marker-and-the-gate-refuses-an-unlisted-bucket.sh: `[tests].run` and `ci.yml`'s full-suite step carry `-m 'not own_records'` and no `--deselect`; the doctor job and the inherit path run `-m own_records`; every `run_doctor(ROOT)` test in `test_doctor.py` carries the marker; the guard reads no deselect list; `attest/buckets.md` lists the five buckets; on a fixture tenant a spec with `Bucket: liveness-by-proxy` is refused naming the missing `buckets.md`, refused again naming the unlisted slug once the file lists another bucket, and passes once the slug is listed, with the refusals written before any criterion ran\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-3VwZG4G3' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-S1R85qN3' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\nBucket: dogfood-tests-told-apart-by-a-list\n\nItem #229's fourth attempt ran 3,375 s and cost $2.62 to fail on one test. The executor's change touched `attavo/common.py` and `attavo/build.py`, `select-tests` mapped that to the whole suite, and the gate ran `tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_invocation_lacks_record` in its worktree, where that test read build-04's own `.started` marker as a dead invocation. The test is one of the seven that read this repository's own records and belong to the doctor job alone. It was the one the deselect lists did not name.\n\nThere were